.EE
.PP
Defaults: structure tokenizer, learn_threshold=1, spike thresholds
3/6/12 (z\-score), parameter changes disabled, stop_factor=3,
away_secs=600.
Frequency spikes and parameter changes are only reported once a profile
has been seen \f[B]learn_threshold\f[R] times.
.PP
\f[B]DetectorConfig\f[R] and \f[B]AnomalyKind\f[R] are
\f[B]#[non_exhaustive]\f[R]: build a config from
\f[B]DetectorConfig::default()\f[R] and assign the fields you need.
.SS AnomalyKind
.IP
.EX
pub enum AnomalyKind {
    NeverBeforeSeen,
    NewInSystem,
    ParameterChange,
    FrequencySpike(SpikeMagnitude),  // Small | Medium | Large
    EventStop,
    SystemAway,
}
.EE
.PP
\f[B]AnomalyKind::as_str()\f[R] returns a stable lowercase identifier
(\f[B]never_before_seen\f[R], \f[B]new_in_system\f[R],
\f[B]parameter_change\f[R], \f[B]frequency_spike\f[R],
\f[B]event_stop\f[R], \f[B]system_away\f[R]).
.SS Profile / ProfileStore
\f[B]Profile\f[R] records what the detector has learned about one
structure on one system: event count, first/last seen timestamps (unix
seconds), per\-position \f[B]ParamTracker\f[R], and inter\-arrival
\f[B]RunningStats\f[R].
.PP
\f[B]ProfileStore\f[R] is the in\-memory (system → hash → Profile) map.
It also tracks which hashes have been seen globally (across all systems)
to enable the \f[B]NeverBeforeSeen\f[R] vs \f[B]NewInSystem\f[R]
distinction.
.SS RunningStats
Online mean/variance accumulator (Welford\[cq]s algorithm) used for
frequency z\-scores.
\f[B]RunningStats::push(x)\f[R] adds a sample; \f[B]zscore(x)\f[R]
returns how many standard deviations \f[I]x\f[R] is from the current
mean.
.SS ParamTracker
Tracks distinct values observed at one parameter slot (the \f[I]n\f[R]th
parameter of the line).
\f[B]ParamTracker::observe(value)\f[R] returns \f[B]true\f[R] when the
value is new.
Past 100 distinct values the slot is \f[I]saturated\f[R]: treated as
free\-form (an id, a counter), it forgets its values and never reports a
change again.
